# No .dockerignore existed before this — `COPY . /app` in Dockerfile stage 2
# was shipping the entire repo into the production image, including multiple
# node_modules trees (frontend/, demo-capture/ [Playwright, ~63MB], scripts/,
# docs/evf/) that the FastAPI backend never imports. Confirmed via
# `grep -rn "frontend|docs/evf|demo-capture|scripts/" main.py` — the backend
# doesn't serve or import any of these; the frontend is a separate Fly.io app
# per docs/ARCHITECTURE.md. This is also what Trivy's node-pkg findings
# (brace-expansion, js-yaml CVEs) were scanning — dev/test-only JS deps that
# were never meant to reach a shipped image.

.git/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
demo-capture/
demo-logs/
demo-logs-a/
demo-logs-b/
.claude/
